 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.76,
   "text": "What if the Earth were made entirely of protons and the Moon were made entirely of electrons?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 4.4,
   "end": 7.66,
   "text": "This is, by far, the most destructive what-if scenario to date.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 8.06,
   "end": 11.04,
   "text": "You might imagine an electron moon orbiting a proton of Earth, sort of like a gigantic",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 11.04,
   "end": 11.78,
   "text": "hydrogen atom.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 12.02,
   "end": 13.22,
   "text": "On one level, it sort of makes sense.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 13.66,
   "end": 15.72,
   "text": "Electrons orbit protons and moons orbit planets.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 16.12,
   "end": 19.22,
   "text": "However, electron moons do not orbit proton planets.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 19.64,
   "end": 22.74,
   "text": "If you put two negatively charged electrons together, they try to fly apart with a force",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 22.74,
   "end": 25.9,
   "text": "about 20 orders of magnitude stronger than the gravity pulling them together.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 26.26,
   "end": 29.98,
   "text": "If you put 10 to the 53 electrons together to build a moon, they push each other apart",
   "avg_logprob": -0.117,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.0
  },
  {
   "start": 29.98,
   "end": 31.5,
   "text": "with an unbelievable amount of energy.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 31.8,
   "end": 35.04,
   "text": "The Moon and Earth would have no chance to gravitationally or even electrostatically",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 35.04,
   "end": 38.52,
   "text": "influence each other, the forces trying to blow each one apart would be far more powerful.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 38.98,
   "end": 42.12,
   "text": "There is a huge amount of potential energy in this scenario, the energy that we imagine",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 42.12,
   "end": 43.58,
   "text": "would blast all those electrons apart.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 43.88,
   "end": 46.28,
   "text": "That energy warps space and time just like mass does.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 46.58,
   "end": 49.96,
   "text": "The amount of energy in our electron moon, it turns out, is about equal to the total",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 49.96,
   "end": 52.26,
   "text": "mass and energy of the entire observable universe.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 52.68,
   "end": 56.14,
   "text": "An entire observable universe where the mass energy concentrated into the space of our",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.014
  },
  {
   "start": 56.14,
   "end": 60.36,
   "text": "relatively small moon would warp space-time so strongly that it would easily overpower",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 60.36,
   "end": 63.06,
   "text": "even the repulsion of those 10 to the 53 electrons.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 63.62,
   "end": 66.36,
   "text": "Would the attraction of this universe mass black hole cause the rest of the universe",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 66.36,
   "end": 66.82,
   "text": "to collapse?",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 67.2,
   "end": 67.92,
   "text": "It's hard to say.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 68.18,
   "end": 71.66,
   "text": "The answer kinda depends on what the deal with dark energy is, and nobody knows what",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 71.66,
   "end": 72.9,
   "text": "the deal with dark energy is.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 73.22,
   "end": 77.76,
   "text": "But for the meantime, at least, nearby galaxies would be safe, since the gravitational influence",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 77.76,
   "end": 80.42,
   "text": "of the black hole can only expand outward at the speed of light.",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 80.88,
   "end": 84.34,
   "text": "Most of the universe around us would remain blissfully unaware of our ridiculous electron",
   "avg_logprob": -0.123,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.105
  },
  {
   "start": 84.34,
   "end": 86.38,
   "text": "experiment until they suddenly...",
   "avg_logprob": -0.635,
   "no_speech_prob": 0.969
  }
 ],
